From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 10:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] RFC (DO NOT SUBMIT): mm: track semantic class at VMA level

/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

Implement the logic to handle MADV_SEMANTIC_* in madvise_vma() and
store the resulting state in vm_flags.

Files likely to be touched:
- include/linux/mm_types.h: Add VM_SEMANTIC_* flags to vm_flags_t.
- mm/madvise.c: Update madvise_behavior_valid() and madvise_vma().

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 include/linux/mm_types.h | 6 ++++++
 mm/madvise.c             | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/mm_types.h b/include/linux/mm_types.h
index [hash]..[hash] 100644
--- a/include/linux/mm_types.h
+++ b/include/linux/mm_types.h
@@ -400,6 +400,12 @@ struct vm_area_struct {
 #define VM_HUGEPAGE	0x01000000	/* Huge pages have been advised */
 #define VM_NOHUGEPAGE	0x02000000	/* No huge pages have been advised */
 
+/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */
+/* Semantic Hints */
+#define VM_SEMANTIC_STREAMING 0x04000000
+#define VM_SEMANTIC_REUSE     0x08000000
+#define VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL 0x10000000
+#define VM_SEMANTIC_MASK      (VM_SEMANTIC_STREAMING | VM_SEMANTIC_REUSE | VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL)
+
 #define VM_MERGEABLE	0x04000000	/* KSM may merge identical pages */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_USES_HIGH_VMA_FLAGS
diff --git a/mm/madvise.c b/mm/madvise.c
index [hash]..[hash] 100644
--- a/mm/madvise.c
+++ b/mm/madvise.c
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ static int madvise_vma_behavior(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 		return madvise_pageout(vma, prev, start, end);
 	case MADV_WILLNEED:
 		return madvise_willneed(vma, prev, start, end);
+	/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */
+	case MADV_SEMANTIC_STREAMING:
+		new_flags |= VM_SEMANTIC_STREAMING;
+		break;
+	case MADV_SEMANTIC_REUSE:
+		new_flags |= VM_SEMANTIC_REUSE;
+		break;
+	case MADV_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL:
+		new_flags |= VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL;
+		break;
 	case MADV_DONTNEED:
 		return madvise_dontneed_free(vma, prev, start, end, behavior);
 	default:
-- 
